(3)shall include a sexual assault victim service provider, such as a rape crisis center, program serving tribal victims of sexual assault, or coalition or other nonprofit nongovernmental organization carrying out a community-based sexual assault program, that has a history of effective work concerning sexual assault and the impact that sexual assault has on children and youth;

(b)Basis of formulaThe formula described in subsection (a) shall be based on the latest available data regarding an area served by a low-income local educational agency on—
 (1)the number of residents under the age of 18 in such area;
 (2)the percentage of the population of such area with incomes below the poverty line;
 (3)the percentage of residents age 18 or older in such area who have earned secondary school diplomas;
 (4)the percentage of students in such area who are identified as eligible for special education services;

